# Detail panel design — Payment Details pattern

When building a **detail sidebar / mobile detail view** (invoice, payment, batch, dispute, etc.), reuse the **Payment Details** composition — not a new modal chrome or card stack.

## Canonical reference

- Component: `src/components/client/PaymentConfirmationPanel.tsx`
- Styles: `.payment-confirmation-panel*` in `src/styles/clientPortal.css`
- Desktop: resizable split pane sidebar (`useResizableSplitPane`)
- Mobile: full-page `variant="mobile"` with back arrow (not a bottom sheet)

## Layout (top → bottom)

1. **Header (compact, `shrink-0`)**
   - Eyebrow: uppercase small label (`Payment details`)
   - Context line: primary entity id (`Invoice 333 · Load …`)
   - Sub line: secondary party (`broker_name`)
   - Actions: prev/next record nav + close (`X` desktop / back on mobile)
   - Padding ~`8px 10px`; icon buttons `28×28`

2. **Status summary (`shrink-0`)**
   - Soft tinted band by status (confirmed green, awaiting amber, disputed red, pending indigo)
   - Optional balance strip (`InvoiceBalanceSummary` with `hideIdentity`)
   - **2×2 meta grid** of compact cells: uppercase `dt` + value `dd`
   - One-line helper / deadline under the grid
   - Keep summary **tight** so the timeline gets the remaining height

3. **Activity & notes (flex grow + scroll)**
   - Section title + filter chips on **one row** (`Activity` / `Notes`)
   - Scrollable list only in this region (`overflow-y: auto`)
   - Note cards: title + date on one row, detail text below
   - Tone classes on titles (`success` / `warning` / `error`)

4. **Footer actions (`shrink-0`, optional)**
   - Primary + secondary buttons (`dashboard-btn-primary` / `dashboard-btn-secondary`)
   - Only when an action is available (e.g. confirm / dispute)

## Density rules (do not regress)

- Prefer **compact** over hero typography — no large display amounts in the header
- Summary padding ~`8px 10px`; meta cells ~`6px 8px`; values ~`0.8125rem`
- Timeline must own vertical space: summary stays short; notes section `flex: 1; min-height: 0`
- Use `tabular-nums` for money and dates
- Status color = meaning only (not decoration on every block)

## Structure recipe

```tsx
<div className="…-panel flex flex-col min-h-0 h-full overflow-hidden">
  <header className="…-panel__header shrink-0">…</header>
  <div className="…-panel__body flex flex-col min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-hidden">
    <section className="…-panel__summary shrink-0">…</section>
    <section className="…-panel__notes flex flex-col min-h-0 flex-1">
      <div className="…-panel__notes-head shrink-0">title + filters</div>
      <div className="…-panel__notes-scroll flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto">…</div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <footer className="…-panel__footer shrink-0">…</footer>
</div>
```

## Do

- Copy BEM-style block naming from `payment-confirmation-panel` (or extract shared `detail-panel` classes later)
- Support `sidebar` + `mobile` variants from one component
- Wire prev/next against the current filtered list order
- Keep identity in the header; don’t repeat invoice # / broker in the summary when `hideIdentity` applies

## Don’t

- Full-screen modal with heavy padding for desktop detail
- Large hero amount + sparse meta that pushes activity off-screen
- Nested cards inside cards in the summary
- Scrolling the whole panel including header/footer — only the notes/timeline scrolls
- Invent a second detail visual language for invoices/batches/disputes
